# Team pipeline (contract + orchestration)

Activate the skill **team-orchestrator** (`.cursor/skills/team-orchestrator/SKILL.md`) for the **full pipeline contract** (every stage’s inputs/outputs, gates, `40-plan.plan.md`). The skill id refers to the folder name; the same file is the reference for **all** `team-pipeline-*` agents when they need I/O details—not only for `team-pipeline-orchestrator`.

**Paths:** `.cursor/…` = under the **workspace root** (opened project), not `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor` (global agents). See skill § **Workspace root**.

Use it when coordinating multi-stage work or when the user invokes pipeline stages one at a time. Per-stage Cursor agents: `team-pipeline-analyst`, `team-pipeline-architect`, `team-pipeline-critical-reviewer`, `team-pipeline-planner`, `team-pipeline-plan-reviewer`, `team-pipeline-developer`, `team-pipeline-code-reviewer`, `team-pipeline-orchestrator` (files under `.cursor/agents/team-pipeline-*.md`).

## Run directory

- Pattern: `.cursor/tasks/runs/<YYYYMMDD>_<short-topic-slug>_<seq>/`
- Resolve via `run=<path>` or `.cursor/tasks/runs/LATEST` (one line = path to active run). Full algorithm: skill **team-orchestrator** § Run directory.
- **`LATEST` is not always this chat’s topic:** if the run came from `LATEST` only, compare with `00-brief.md` — **new subject → new run folder**, do not overwrite another audit (skill § **Same run vs new run**). `run=<path>` = explicit choice.
- **Analyst** and **orchestrator** may **bootstrap** a new run + `LATEST` when the skill’s conditions match; other stages must not auto-create runs if the path is unknown.

## Modes

- **full:** analyst → architect → critical-reviewer → planner → plan_reviewer → developer → code_reviewer
- **fast:** analyst → planner → developer (optional code_reviewer); planner must document assumptions in `40-plan.plan.md`

## File I/O by stage (run-relative)

| Stage | Read | Write |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| analyst | `00-brief.md` | `10-analyst.md`, `manifest.json` |
| architect | `10-analyst.md` | `20-architecture.md`, `manifest.json` |
| critical-reviewer | `10-analyst.md`, `20-architecture.md` | `30-critical-review.md`, `manifest.json` |
| planner (full) | `10-analyst.md`, `20-architecture.md`, optional `30-critical-review.md` | `40-plan.plan.md`, `manifest.json` |
| planner (fast) | `10-analyst.md` | `40-plan.plan.md`, `manifest.json` |
| plan_reviewer | `40-plan.plan.md` | `50-plan-review.md`, `manifest.json` |
| developer (full) | `40-plan.plan.md`, `50-plan-review.md` | code + `60-implementation-notes.md`, `manifest.json` |
| developer (fast) | `40-plan.plan.md` | code + `60-implementation-notes.md`, `manifest.json` |
| code_reviewer | `60-implementation-notes.md` | `70-code-review.md`, `manifest.json` |

Before each stage: verify required input files exist; if not, stop and name the missing producer stage.

**Artifact completeness:** Stage markdown files (`10-` … `70-`) must contain the **full** report for that invocation, not a stub while detail lives only in chat — see skill **team-orchestrator** § **Artifact completeness (all pipeline markdown outputs)**.

## Optional specialists

Extra `Task` subagent types (per project rules) may slot in after planning or where `40-plan.plan.md` specifies—never required by this rule; keep artifacts in the same run folder.

## Orchestration

Use `Task` with one `subagent_type` per call. Pass the run directory path and the exact read/write filenames from the skill.
